    <h1>RGT Drivers: a medical courier run from a phone</h1>
    <p>RGT Drivers is a courier and medical delivery company in Silver Spring, Maryland. It’s where Neo was built, and where every module runs before we offer it to anyone else.</p>
  </div>
  <section style="padding-top:1rem">
    <article class="prose">
      <p class="muted"><strong>Disclosure:</strong> RGT Drivers is owned by Rudy Baptiste, the founder of Brightview Agency.</p>

      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p>Like most small courier companies, RGT’s owner was the receptionist, the dispatcher and the bookkeeper. Calls came in while he was driving, rush pickups needed assigning late at night, and every week ended with a payroll spreadsheet.</p>

      <h2>What Neo does at RGT today</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Dispatch:</strong> creates and assigns delivery jobs in Shipday from a plain-English request, with RGT’s order numbering.</li>
        <li><strong>Late-delivery monitor:</strong> watches active jobs and raises an alert when one is running late.</li>
        <li><strong>Proof of delivery:</strong> emails customers a delivery report with photos automatically.</li>
        <li><strong>Weekly routes and payroll:</strong> builds recurring route orders and the weekly driver settlement sheet.</li>
        <li><strong>Front desk:</strong> answers the phone, texts back missed callers, and replies to every website form and emailed lead in under a minute, with follow-ups on days 1, 3 and 7.</li>
        <li><strong>Knowledge base:</strong> quotes from RGT’s own rate sheet, which the owner updates from Telegram.</li>
        <li><strong>Approval mode:</strong> marketing texts, bulk messages and unusual invoices wait for one tap; rush jobs never do.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the owner works now</h2>
      <p>Everything Neo does is copied to the owner on Telegram. He approves what matters with a tap, asks for reports in plain English, and spends his time on customers and drivers instead of data entry.</p>

      <h2>Medical privacy</h2>
      <p>Texts carry times and order numbers only; no patient details ever go by text.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:2rem"><a href="/book?industry=Courier" class="btn-primary">See Neo for your business</a></p>
    </article>
  </section>
